Output: 3 5173 7Time Complexity: O(log n), for each query.The precomputation for smallest prime factor is done in O(n log log n) using sieve. Whereas in the calculation step we are dividing the number every time by the smallest prime number till it becomes 1. So, let's consider a worst case in which every time the SPF is 2 . Therefore will have log n division steps. Hence, We can say that our Time Complexity will be O(log n) in worst case.Auxiliary Space: O(1)Note : The above code works well for n up to the order of 10^7. Beyond this we will face memory issues.
